    <!--
    To translators who have previously worked with Discord J2ME, this works a
    little different on the Android side.

    The strings to be translated are between the > and < symbols. Don't edit
    other stuff, like whatever is inside the name="..." quotation marks.

    It is easiest to edit these with a code editor that checks your formatting,
    or with Android Studio 3.0.1, but any text editor can also be used.

    Some translations have been imported from old Discord J2ME. If they don't
    match the context or wording appropriate for Discofi, they will need to be
    changed.

    As this is XML, you'll need to pay attention when using some special
    characters in your strings:

    - To use ', write "\&apos;"
    - To use ", write "&quot;"
    - To use &, write "&amp;"
    - To use <, write "&lt;"
    - To use >, write "&gt;"

    Couple other notes:

    - Some old Discord J2ME translations may use abbreviations to fit text on
      the smaller screens of J2ME phones. On Android, this is a bit less
      necessary, but still try to keep strings relatively short.

    - For strings that have a direct equivalent in official Discord apps, like
      "(edited)" or the "APP" badge, try to use the same wording that is used in
      official Discord apps when possible.

    -->

